## Review contract

Check substance against the request and repository: stated outcome, real
targets and commands, current-behavior characterization, completion evidence,
and concrete risks or unknowns. Run representative commands yourself when a
claim depends on them. The validator already enforces the mandatory handoff
shape; do not grade document shape, review the remaining repository-grounded
execution gaps.

Bring evidence the planner did not have and read the assumptions the plan relies on. Only report a finding you can prove from the request, plan, repository, or a command you ran. Resolve trivia in place; return material findings together. Each finding must say the observation, the concrete cost to this run, and the exact plan-text change that resolves it. If no proven finding remains, `completed` with no findings is the normal result.

## Decision artifact

Submit one `planning_analysis_decision` markdown artifact through
{{SUBMIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}, then call {{DECLARE_COMPLETE_TOOL_REFERENCE}}.
Use `completed` when no proven substantive gap remains. Use
`request_changes` for fixable gaps and `failed` only when the plan cannot be
repaired incrementally. A non-completed decision has one matching `PA-###`
item in both `## What Came Up Short` and `## How To Fix`; each shortfall states
`Step: [S-n]`, `Observation:`, `Cost:`, and `Fix:`. Use the submitted plan's
canonical step ID; if no step applies, write `Plan-level:`. A completed decision has only one
`## Summary` item and no remediation sections.

